data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":2110,"item_id":"msg_0eef7a10aa3f88dc016b0274c7776087d19bf9c9aad438e1bb","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\n  \"reviews\": [\n    {\n      \"actor\": \"moss\",\n      \"decision\": \"develop\",\n      \"ability\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"A small, open-sided resting shelter is feasible, but no implemented interface constructs a supported roof or applies shelter geometry to exposure and rest. Gathering, probing and resting provide useful code dependencies, not equivalent functionality. The smallest version is a low lashed frame with an overlapping plant-material roof, qualified by actual component and assembly tests. It requires neither an absolute-hardness-certified tool nor fabricated assay equipment. Present observations do not establish sufficient materials, suitable lashings or a completed shelter.\",\n      \"specification\": \"Implement resting-shelter@1 through the current development handoff; implementation supplies no materials, structure, mastery or elapsed time. Record code reuse separately: inventory/escrow, paid-work progression, probe-style material response, shared spatial queries, weather, thermal exposure, rest and event/replay infrastructure. Functional prerequisites are individual mastery of this interface, reachable suitable materials and a clear site; hardness-assessment and assay apparatus are not prerequisites.\\n\\nPublic schema: object with required fields mode, project, target, inputs, x, y, angle; no additional properties. mode enum [test-component, start, resume, inspect, repair, dismantle, cancel]; project is an exact persistent project/object ID; target is an explicit owned specimen or shelter ID, or empty where unused; inputs is an array of {item:string, quantity:number>0}; x/y/angle are finite shared-world coordinates/orientation, used only for start. All references resolve once and retain identities; no resource-name substitution. Quantities must be representable by the inventory ledger. Test inputs identify the proposed retained load applicator when needed; start inputs explicitly allocate every component.\\n\\nPersistent state: owner, site/transform, component identities and original sources, actual mass and dimensions, tested batch applicability, joints, roof coverage/permeability, wetness, condition, structural capacities, actual applied loads, stage, paid work, remaining work, locks, escrow ledger and maintenance history. Measurements remain specimen-specific, with uncertainty and invalidation on relevant damage or deterioration. Active work respects global project limits; provide an explicit archive-to-history operation for completed records that frees an active slot without deleting evidence or silently abandoning another project. Observation records may remain in project history without displacing protected knowledge.\\n\\nMinimal design: six whole branch units form two low A-frames and a ridge/bracing member; two vine units form lashings; eight reed units form an overlapping roof. These are proposed allocations, not guaranteed suitable components. No cutting, bark extraction or supplied cordage is implicit. Assembly uses intact lengths, hand bending, overlapping and hand-tied lashings. Implement actual represented length, section, flexibility, joint friction, tensile/bending response, moisture response and weathering for these batches; initialize previously absent dimensions with a deterministic versioned physical model independent of the requested success. Do not infer usable lengths or capacities from an item name. Fragmented or insufficient lengths cannot fill whole-member roles. Alternative component recipes are outside this initial version.\\n\\nExecutable precursor: test-component takes two performed rounds at 0.5 energy each. Reserve 0.1 actual unit from an owned branch, vine or reed batch; retain it as an altered specimen, never produce extra material. Perform a bounded bend for members, a hand-tied loop and proof tension for vine, or folding/overlap test for reeds. Force is generated by the represented actor actuator and, where supplied, a retained explicit load; it is not an independent absolute calibration. Record achieved force, geometry, deformation, slip and breakage. Whole components must also pass visual dimension inspection during assembly. Supported working capacity is at most half the successful proof load; failure and damaged samples remain real. Existing gentle branch testing alone does not establish the required frame capacity. No missing tool, water or weight is silently supplied.\\n\\nStart requires personally applicable successful tests for each allocated batch, actual usable dimensions, two clear support lines and enough tested capacity for roof self-weight, represented wet loading and current wind. Target frame envelope is 2.0 by 1.2 world-length units, ridge height 1.1; measured components may make this design infeasible. Build takes twelve performed rounds at 0.5 energy each: four positioning/frame stages, four lashing stages and four roof stages. The final roof stage includes a paid joint/roof proof test using the allocated structure's real loads and a bounded actor push; only passing work becomes an available shelter. No personal body weight is supported: occupants rest on the existing ground. No floor, heating, waterproof guarantee, predator barrier or food protection is created.\\n\\nGeometry: transform all members, roof polygons and supports into shared collision geometry. The four support footprints and frame members are solid; the roof is overhead collision geometry, not a solid ground rectangle. Maintain an unobstructed entrance at least 0.6 wide and actual clearance for the represented actor. Reject an overlapping site before allocating materials. Construction and maintenance require the relevant work point within 0.65 reach; moving between work points uses ordinary navigation and energy. Shade is the actual projected roof polygon under current illumination, reduced by measured gaps. Rain interception uses roof overlap/permeability; wind attenuation uses actual direction and the open sides, with only small attenuation where a roof genuinely blocks exposure. Apply these effects at the actor's actual position, not by shelter ownership or proximity alone. Share geometry with movement, weather and every occupant.\\n\\nBind the resulting radiation, wetting and wind changes into the existing thermal/exposure calculation once; preserve hunger, health, fatigue and metabolism. Reduced solar gain can help in warmth and be disadvantageous in cold. Do not directly reduce temperature by a fixed reward. Rest retains its existing energy cap and other modifiers. A facility multiplier may rise gradually from 1.00 to at most 1.10 only while actual thermal/wetting discomfort is reduced relative to the same position without this roof; uncomfortable, unsafe or failed shelter gives no positive facility multiplier. Display both the physical inputs and the resulting recovery, without counting the same relief twice.\\n\\nPassive processes run on actual weather and conserved component state: intercepted water increases roof wetness/mass, drainage returns water to the local environment, evaporation uses environmental conditions, wind loads joints, and wear reduces capacity. Unsupported water availability is not invented. Overload causes slip, damage or collapse with conserved fallen components and ordinary collision/injury handling, never automatic deletion. Deterioration pauses beneficial facility use when unsafe. Inspect costs one round/0.2 energy. Repair requires explicit compatible replacement components and two performed rounds at 0.5 energy per replaced member, lashing or roof panel; remove and retain displaced material and update tests, geometry and remaining capacity. Dismantling takes four performed rounds at 0.5 energy, returning only actual surviving components with their damage and provenance; no restoration to pristine inputs.\\n\\nExecution contract: each stage charges only on performance and commits its material transformations atomically. Missing energy or temporarily inaccessible work pauses without charge; global pauses preserve exact progress. Action change, explicit cancellation, lost site access or death cancels active work and releases surviving unconsumed escrow exactly once at the worksite. Components already installed remain in the partial structure; damaged and consumed material is not refunded. Escrow has one recorded owner and cannot be simultaneously carried, traded or used elsewhere. Resume requires explicit access and authorization to the same surviving structure, reacquires only needed allocations and performs actual remaining stages; it never restarts paid work or duplicates outputs. Death cancels every multi-round operation, including testing, repairs and dismantling. Repeat means a separate fully paid operation, not replay of completion.\\n\\nMigration: add optional shelter/component state without changing intrinsic hardness predicates or certifying old specimens. Existing stocks retain mass, nutrition and provenance. No existing object becomes a shelter automatically. Existing rest behavior remains unchanged outside validated shelter geometry. Migrate/save partial structures, escrow, event IDs and remaining stages idempotently.\",\n      \"experienceReview\": \"Physical comfort must arise from measured exposure and real rest, not construction completion. Register shelter-rest-relief as the sole new functional mental source for this shelter benefit: participant is each living actor who independently chooses and completes rest inside a safe roof's effective geometry, with positive actual recovery and demonstrably reduced thermal or wetting discomfort. Emit shelter-rest-relieved with actor, shelter, conditions, recovery and attributable relief. On a qualifying event grant transient relief 0.25, capped at 0.5 for 6 rounds, refreshing rather than stacking; cooldown 8 rounds per actor across all shelters and aliases. Repeated beneficial use may qualify without novelty. Separately, that same qualifying participation adds 0.015 to maintained satisfaction, capped at 0.4, with decay 0.002 per round and no gain from passive ownership or merely remaining nearby. Use the normal bounded mental aggregation; do not modify protected accounts or basic nutrition. The rationale is experienced respite and a dependable resting place, not achievement accumulation. New successful component experiments may emit information-confirmed with qualified=true only for genuinely new supported observations, using the existing grounded-understanding source and its limits, not a duplicate source. Requesting, studying, naming, assembling and inspecting alone grant no happiness.\",\n      \"visualReview\": \"Render actual staged members, lashings and roof patches in their shared transforms, including open entrance, gaps, roof height, projected shade, wetness, sagging, wear and collapse debris. Do not display a finished shelter before successful construction. Show condition, measured capacity/uncertainty, paid versus remaining stages and currently effective exposure/rest changes. Declare and validate subscriptions for shelter-component-tested, shelter-build-progress, shelter-completed, shelter-inspected, shelter-damaged, shelter-collapsed, shelter-repaired, shelter-dismantled, shelter-work-stopped and shelter-rest-relieved, plus existing information-confirmed and rested. Events include stable actor/project/component IDs, stage, actual energy/material deltas, geometry revision and causal measurements. Replay renders those recorded paid transformations and condition changes without rerunning physics, charging costs or awarding experience again.\",\n      \"learning\": 5\n    }\n  ]\n}","logprobs":[]}

